### Configure Tauri Build Commands for Vite

Source: https://v2.tauri.app/start/frontend/vite

Configures Tauri's build settings to integrate with Vite, defining beforeDevCommand, beforeBuildCommand, devUrl, and frontendDist. Examples are provided for npm, yarn, pnpm, and Deno.

```json
{
  "build": {
    "beforeDevCommand": "npm run dev",
    "beforeBuildCommand": "npm run build",
    "devUrl": "http://localhost:5173",
    "frontendDist": "../dist"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "build": {
    "beforeDevCommand": "yarn dev",
    "beforeBuildCommand": "yarn build",
    "devUrl": "http://localhost:5173",
    "frontendDist": "../dist"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "build": {
    "beforeDevCommand": "pnpm dev",
    "beforeBuildCommand": "pnpm build",
    "devUrl": "http://localhost:5173",
    "frontendDist": "../dist"
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "build": {
    "beforeDevCommand": "deno task dev",
    "beforeBuildCommand": "deno task build",
    "devUrl": "http://localhost:5173",
    "frontendDist": "../dist"
  }
}
```

### Vite > Example configuration > Update Tauri configuration

Source: https://v2.tauri.app/start/frontend/vite

The Tauri CLI can be configured to utilize your Vite development server and `dist` folder. This includes setting `beforeDevCommand` to run `npm run dev` (or equivalent for other package managers) and `beforeBuildCommand` to run `npm run build`, with `devUrl` pointing to `http://localhost:5173` and `frontendDist` set to `../dist`.

--------------------------------

### BuildConfig > Frontend and Development

Source: https://v2.tauri.app/reference/config

The development environment can load assets from a dev server URL or a local directory. If a path is provided for frontend distribution, Tauri embeds the files into the application binary and serves them from a default entry point. Alternatively, providing a remote URL allows the application to load content without bundled assets.

